# The place Russian р is spoken at, which the English module this one is a
# copy of has not got. English r is retroflex: its locus, eng_ret_Fv, brings
# the third formant down to 1650 and 1600, and that low third formant is the
# whole of what makes it sound American. Russian р is alveolar, like Spanish
# r, and the numbers below are Spanish's own, read off span_trill_Fv in
# lang/eses: f2 1250, f3 2300 into the sound and 2100 out of it, f4 2800 and
# f5 3600. The first formant is ga_ph_r's to set and it sets it before it
# asks for a place, so nothing here touches it.
#
# The first three lines are eng_ret_Fv's own and are kept so that whatever
# that rule set from state+2802 the r still has: the locus is the only thing
# that changes.
rule ru_trill_Fv takes 1 from es_val.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  raw load movw statefld 2802 into r0w
  raw alu addw imm 100 reg r0w
  raw store movw reg r0w statefld 2894
  set global half 3086 to 1250
  set global half 3090 to 1250
  set global half 3094 to 2300
  set global half 3098 to 2100
  set global half 3102 to 2800
  set global half 3110 to 3600
  match
end
